---
import BaseLayout from '../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Intelligence consulting and narrative strategy"
  description="I help organisations implement Editorial Intelligence — building the narrative systems, evidence workflows and editorial capability that turn distributed knowledge into a compounding strategic asset."
>
  <article class="container-site py-20">
    <div class="work-inner">

      <!-- Hero -->
      <header class="mb-12">
        <p class="t-label mb-6">Work with me</p>
        <h1 class="t-display mb-6">Start with what you know.<br />Find out what you need to learn.</h1>
        <div class="prose-section mb-8">
          <p>I help B2B research, thought-leadership and content leaders generate and develop evidence, then turn it into distinctive positions, stronger editorial programmes and knowledge that compounds.</p>
          <p>Some organisations already hold valuable research, customer insight and expertise. Others need to generate evidence before they can build a credible position. Editorial Intelligence supports both starting points.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="engagement-signal mb-8">Most projects are fixed-scope engagements delivered over two to eight weeks.</p>
        <div class="hero-ctas">
          <a href="mailto:asavin@editorialintelligence.co?subject=Editorial%20Intelligence%20project%20enquiry" class="work-btn">Discuss what you need to understand</a>
          <a href="#services" class="work-link">Explore the services ↓</a>
        </div>
      </header>

      <!-- Services -->
      <section id="services" class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="t-label mb-4">Ways to work together</h2>
        <div class="prose-section mb-10">
          <p>Start by understanding what you know and what is missing. Develop existing evidence or generate what is needed, then build the narrative, activation system or specialist application the opportunity requires.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="work-routes mb-12">
          <a href="#understand" class="work-route">
            <span class="work-route-number">01</span>
            <h3>Understand what you already know</h3>
            <p>Review existing research, customer insight, expertise and content to find the argument, evidence gaps and opportunities already present.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="#generate" class="work-route">
            <span class="work-route-number">02</span>
            <h3>Generate the evidence you need</h3>
            <p>Investigate an important question through focused qualitative research, interviews and structured practitioner conversations.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="#develop" class="work-route">
            <span class="work-route-number">03</span>
            <h3>Develop and activate the argument</h3>
            <p>Turn evidence into a distinctive position, narrative system and the formats needed to make it useful.</p>
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- Flagship: Narrative audit -->
        <div id="understand" class="service-flagship mb-12">
          <p class="service-eyebrow">Route 1 · Understand what you already know</p>
          <h3 class="service-heading">Narrative audit</h3>
          <p class="service-prop">Find out what your existing evidence actually adds up to.</p>
          <div class="prose-section mb-6">
            <p>A structured review of your research, content, customer insight and market evidence. I identify the strongest argument already present, assess what genuinely supports it and show where valuable signals are being missed.</p>
            <p>The audit is designed for organisations that know they are sitting on useful material but do not yet have a clear view of the narrative opportunity.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="service-includes mb-6">
            <p class="service-includes-label">Includes</p>
            <ul class="work-list">
              <li>The strongest through-lines across your existing material</li>
              <li>The evidence with the greatest strategic value</li>
              <li>Gaps, contradictions and overlooked signals</li>
              <li>Existing assets worth reactivating</li>
              <li>The narrative territories you could credibly own</li>
              <li>Recommended priorities for further development</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="what-you-leave mb-6">
            <p class="what-you-leave-label">What you leave with</p>
            <p class="what-you-leave-desc">A clear view of the strongest argument already present in your material, the evidence that supports it, the gaps that weaken it and the narrative opportunities worth developing.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="engagement-outcome">Deliverable: a concise narrative audit, evidence map and opportunity brief. Fixed scope and fixed fee. Typically completed within two to three weeks.</p>
          <a href="/work/narrative-audit" class="work-btn mt-6 inline-flex">Explore the Narrative Audit</a>
        </div>

        <div class="service-specialist mb-12">
          <p class="service-section-label mb-6">For B2B startups and early scaleups</p>
          <h3 class="service-heading-sm">Startup Narrative Audit</h3>
          <p class="service-prop-sm">Turn founder conviction, customer learning and product evidence into a position your company can defend and test.</p>
          <div class="prose-section-sm mb-4">
            <p>This focused audit connects what different parts of a growing company are learning, distinguishes evidence from assumption and identifies the strongest argument worth developing next.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="what-you-leave mb-4">
            <p class="what-you-leave-label">What you leave with</p>
            <p class="what-you-leave-desc-sm">A narrative diagnosis, evidence and assumption map, core argument, priority opportunities and a 90-day activation and learning plan.</p>
          </div>
          <a href="/work/startup-narrative-audit" class="service-inline-link">Explore the Startup Narrative Audit →</a>
        </div>

        <div id="generate" class="service-specialist mb-12">
          <p class="service-section-label mb-6">Route 2 · Generate the evidence you need</p>
          <h3 class="service-heading-sm">Research-led thought leadership</h3>
          <p class="service-prop-sm">Generate original evidence and turn it into a distinctive argument, report and content programme.</p>
          <div class="prose-section-sm mb-4">
            <p>For organisations with an important market question but insufficient original evidence to answer it credibly. I design a focused qualitative enquiry, gather evidence through interviews and structured conversations, then synthesise the findings into a point of view the organisation can use.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="what-you-leave mb-4">
            <p class="what-you-leave-label">What you leave with</p>
            <p class="what-you-leave-desc-sm">An evidence base, a defensible central argument, a flagship report and a practical plan for extending the thinking across articles, executive content, events and future research.</p>
          </div>
          <a href="/work/research-led-thought-leadership" class="service-inline-link">Explore research-led thought leadership →</a>
        </div>

        <!-- Build layer -->
        <div id="develop" class="mb-12">
          <p class="service-section-label mb-8">Route 3 · Develop and activate the argument</p>
          <div class="service-dev-grid">

            <!-- Research activation -->
            <div class="service-dev-card">
              <h3 class="service-heading-sm">Research activation</h3>
              <p class="service-prop-sm">Your research should produce more than a report.</p>
              <div class="prose-section-sm mb-4">
                <p>For organisations that have commissioned original research and need it to work harder.</p>
                <p>I turn the findings into a clear strategic argument, determine which evidence matters most and design a structure through which the research can support thought leadership, editorial content, executive communications, webinars, events and future research.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="what-you-leave mb-4">
                <p class="what-you-leave-label">What you leave with</p>
                <p class="what-you-leave-desc-sm">A clear research narrative, an evidence hierarchy and a practical activation system for thought leadership, executive communications, webinars, events and future content.</p>
              </div>
              <p class="engagement-outcome">Deliverable: a research narrative and activation system.</p>
              <a href="/narratives/hidden-hours" class="service-inline-link">See how this works through Hidden Hours →</a>
            </div>

            <!-- Thought leadership architecture -->
            <div class="service-dev-card">
              <h3 class="service-heading-sm">Thought leadership architecture</h3>
              <p class="service-prop-sm">Turn organisational expertise into a position the market can recognise.</p>
              <div class="prose-section-sm mb-4">
                <p>For organisations with credible expertise, evidence and opinions but no coherent market position connecting them.</p>
                <p>I bring together research, customer experience, executive expertise and market signals to define the problem the organisation can own, its distinctive interpretation and the evidence required to sustain it.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="what-you-leave mb-4">
                <p class="what-you-leave-label">What you leave with</p>
                <p class="what-you-leave-desc-sm">A distinctive strategic position, the evidence and proprietary ideas that support it, and an editorial architecture through which the organisation can develop it consistently.</p>
              </div>
              <p class="engagement-outcome">Deliverable: a thought leadership platform and editorial architecture.</p>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- AI Visibility Audit -->
        <div class="service-flagship mb-12">
          <p class="service-eyebrow">A focused application</p>
          <h3 class="service-heading">AI Visibility Audit</h3>
          <p class="service-prop">Understand how AI systems describe your organisation, where competitors hold stronger authority and what evidence, narratives and knowledge structures could improve your visibility.</p>
          <div class="prose-section mb-6">
            <p>AI visibility is not created by optimisation. It is created by connected, evidenced, distinctive knowledge that AI systems can understand and trust. The audit assesses where your authority is strong, where it is fragmented and what practical changes would make the most difference.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="what-you-leave mb-6">
            <p class="what-you-leave-label">What you leave with</p>
            <p class="what-you-leave-desc">An AI visibility baseline, competitor comparison, evidence and authority map, narrative gap analysis, knowledge-system assessment and a prioritised 90-day roadmap.</p>
          </div>
          <a href="/work/ai-visibility-audit" class="work-btn mt-6 inline-flex">Explore the AI Visibility Audit</a>
        </div>

        <!-- Webinars, speeches and events -->
        <div class="service-specialist mb-12">
          <p class="service-section-label mb-6">A specialist application</p>
          <h3 class="service-heading-sm">Webinars, speeches and events</h3>
          <p class="service-prop-sm">Shape what the event says—and make what it reveals useful afterwards.</p>
          <div class="prose-section-sm mb-4">
            <p>I can develop the argument for a webinar, speech, panel or event presentation, then carry it through into scripts, slides, speaker notes, moderator questions and supporting editorial material.</p>
            <p>The work can also continue after the session: analysing speaker expertise, audience questions, poll findings and points of tension to create an evidence bank, follow-up content and questions for future research.</p>
            <p>This is editorial development and activation, not event management, technical production or promotion.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="what-you-leave mb-4">
            <p class="what-you-leave-label">What you leave with</p>
            <p class="what-you-leave-desc-sm">A clear event argument and the materials needed to deliver it, with an optional evidence and activation plan for extending the value beyond the live session.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="engagement-outcome mb-3">Deliverables may include a narrative brief, webinar or speech script, slide deck, speaker notes, moderator guide, event intelligence report and activation plan.</p>
          <a href="/experiments/event-intelligence" class="service-inline-link">See how events become reusable intelligence →</a>
        </div>

        <!-- Executive thought leadership and social activation -->
        <div class="service-specialist mb-12">
          <p class="service-section-label mb-6">A specialist application</p>
          <h3 class="service-heading-sm">Executive thought leadership and social activation</h3>
          <p class="service-prop-sm">Turn genuine expertise into a credible voice people can recognise over time.</p>
          <div class="prose-section-sm mb-4">
            <p>I work with executives and subject-matter experts to extract their strongest ideas, connect them to evidence and experience, and develop recurring narrative themes for LinkedIn and other editorial channels.</p>
            <p>The work can include interviews, voice development, ghostwritten posts and articles, editorial planning, and the social activation of research, reports, events and campaigns. Audience response becomes evidence for refining the position rather than merely a performance score.</p>
            <p>This is editorial and narrative development, not routine community moderation, customer service, paid-media operation or platform administration.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="what-you-leave mb-4">
            <p class="what-you-leave-label">What you leave with</p>
            <p class="what-you-leave-desc-sm">A defensible executive point of view, a recognisable voice, recurring narrative themes and publishable material grounded in real expertise.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="engagement-outcome">Deliverables may include an executive narrative brief, voice guide, interview-led LinkedIn posts and articles, an evidence-led editorial plan and an activation learning memo.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Editorial applications -->
        <div class="service-specialist mb-12">
          <p class="service-section-label mb-6">Editorial judgement applied</p>
          <h3 class="service-heading-sm">The output follows the argument</h3>
          <p class="service-prop-sm">Writing is an output. Editorial judgement is the service.</p>
          <div class="prose-section-sm mb-4">
            <p>I can carry the evidence and narrative through into the form the work requires. That may be a video script and production brief, a report, a pitch deck, an interactive diagnostic or executive social content.</p>
            <p>The work begins by deciding what matters, what the evidence supports and what the audience needs—not by filling a format. Newsletters, award entries and bids are also available where the same evidence-led judgement is useful.</p>
          </div>
          <a href="/applications#editorial-outputs" class="service-inline-link">Explore how judgement shapes different outputs →</a>
        </div>

        <!-- Editorial Intelligence programme -->
        <div class="service-flagship mb-12">
          <p class="service-eyebrow">The broadest engagement</p>
          <h3 class="service-heading">Editorial Intelligence programme</h3>
          <p class="service-prop">Build the system that connects evidence, narrative and content — and keeps learning after each project ends.</p>
          <div class="prose-section mb-6">
            <p>For organisations that want more than a single project. A programme connects evidence generation, insight, narrative development, editorial workflows, content creation, activation and measurement into one operating system, so what the organisation learns becomes a reusable asset rather than a series of disconnected deliverables.</p>
            <p>Each element can still be commissioned on its own. The programme is for teams ready to make the connections permanent — a shared evidence base, a narrative architecture the whole team can work from and workflows that improve with use.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="service-includes mb-6">
            <p class="service-includes-label">Can include</p>
            <ul class="work-list">
              <li>An audit of existing evidence, narratives and editorial workflows</li>
              <li>Evidence generation where important questions remain unanswered</li>
              <li>A narrative architecture connecting research, expertise and customer insight</li>
              <li>Editorial workflows, AI prompts and knowledge structures your team can reuse</li>
              <li>Activation across the formats the argument requires</li>
              <li>Measurement and review cadences that turn results into new evidence</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="what-you-leave mb-6">
            <p class="what-you-leave-label">What you leave with</p>
            <p class="what-you-leave-desc">An editorial operating system your team runs: connected evidence, a narrative the organisation can defend, repeatable workflows and knowledge that compounds instead of resetting with every campaign.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="engagement-outcome">Scoped in phases, with each phase useful and complete on its own. The methodology is documented — and continuously tested — through the Editorial Intelligence OS.</p>
          <a href="/editorial-intelligence-os" class="work-btn mt-6 inline-flex">See the operating system behind the programme</a>
        </div>

        <!-- Advisory -->
        <div class="service-advisory">
          <p class="service-section-label mb-6">Continue the work</p>
          <h3 class="service-heading-sm">Editorial Intelligence advisory</h3>
          <p class="service-prop-sm">An ongoing editorial perspective on what your evidence means and where the narrative should go next.</p>
          <div class="prose-section-sm mb-4">
            <p>For teams that need continuing strategic judgement rather than another production retainer.</p>
            <p>The advisory relationship can include reviewing new research, connecting new evidence to existing narratives, challenging content plans, identifying emerging signals and deciding when the strategic argument needs to evolve.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="what-you-leave mb-4">
            <p class="what-you-leave-label">What you leave with</p>
            <p class="what-you-leave-desc-sm">Continuing senior editorial judgement on what new evidence means, how it connects to the existing position and where the narrative should develop next.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="engagement-outcome mb-4">Retainer-based, with the scope defined around the organisation's needs.</p>
          <a href="mailto:asavin@editorialintelligence.co?subject=Editorial%20Intelligence%20project%20enquiry" class="work-btn">Discuss ongoing advisory</a>
        </div>

      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <!-- Proof -->
      <section class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="t-label mb-4">The practice behind the services</h2>
        <div class="prose-section mb-10">
          <p>This work is grounded in two decades of editorial and content experience in complex B2B markets: developing research-led narratives, turning customer insight into useful evidence and connecting organisational knowledge into systems that outlast individual campaigns.</p>
          <p>The work documented across this site shows the methodology in practice.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="proof-items">
          <a href="/narratives/hidden-hours" class="proof-item group">
            <div class="proof-item-inner">
              <p class="proof-label">Hidden Hours — Sage</p>
              <p class="proof-desc">How one research programme was extended beyond its original report into an ongoing narrative platform, editorial series, diagnostic concept and source of market intelligence.</p>
              <span class="proof-link group-hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] transition-colors">Explore →</span>
            </div>
          </a>
          <a href="/narratives/winning-in-small" class="proof-item group">
            <div class="proof-item-inner">
              <p class="proof-label">Winning in Small — Sage</p>
              <p class="proof-desc">How event insight, customer stories and survey evidence were synthesised into a clearer strategic argument.</p>
              <span class="proof-link group-hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] transition-colors">Explore →</span>
            </div>
          </a>
          <a href="/applications" class="proof-item group">
            <div class="proof-item-inner">
              <p class="proof-label">Applications</p>
              <p class="proof-desc">How Editorial Intelligence can be applied across research, events, customer evidence, AI workflows and editorial activation.</p>
              <span class="proof-link group-hover:text-[var(--color-accent)] transition-colors">Explore →</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <!-- Distinction -->
      <section class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="t-label mb-6">A small, senior practice</h2>
        <div class="prose-section">
          <p>I am not an agency. I work on a small number of engagements at a time, which means the analysis, synthesis and strategic thinking are carried out by me rather than delegated through a larger team.</p>
          <p>The work is particularly suited to established B2B organisations, startups and scaleups in fintech, SaaS, professional services and other complex markets where credibility depends on connecting evidence with genuine subject expertise.</p>
          <p>For startups, Editorial Intelligence can also help build and test the initial position before a large body of evidence has accumulated. <a href="/applications/startups-scaleups" class="work-inline-link">Explore Editorial Intelligence for startups and scaleups →</a></p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <!-- Final CTA -->
      <section class="mb-8">
        <h2 class="t-label mb-6">Start with the question</h2>
        <div class="prose-section mb-8">
          <p>Tell me what you are trying to understand or communicate. I’ll help you assess the evidence you already have, identify what is missing and decide what is worth developing.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="mailto:asavin@editorialintelligence.co?subject=Editorial%20Intelligence%20project%20enquiry" class="contact-cta">
          asavin@editorialintelligence.co
          <span class="contact-cta-arrow">→</span>
        </a>
        <p class="work-research-route">Not looking for a project? If you are exploring similar questions in your own work, you can also <a href="/compare-notes">compare notes with me →</a></p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .work-inner {
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  .work-routes {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--color-rule);
  }

  .work-route {
    display: block;
    padding: 1.35rem;
    background: var(--color-surface-secondary);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.15s;
  }

  .work-route:hover {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 7%, var(--color-surface-secondary));
  }

  .work-route-number {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.625rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .work-route h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.55rem;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .work-route p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-ink-secondary);
  }

  .work-research-route { margin-top: 1.25rem; font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--color-ink-tertiary); }
  .work-research-route a { color: var(--color-accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .work-research-route a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  /* ── Prose ── */
  .prose-section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .prose-section p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--color-ink-secondary);
  }

  .prose-section-sm {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .prose-section-sm p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-ink-secondary);
  }

  .engagement-signal {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-ink-tertiary);
    border-left: 2px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 55%, transparent);
    padding-left: 0.875rem;
  }

  /* ── Lists ── */
  .work-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .work-list li {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-ink-secondary);
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .work-list li::before {
    content: '→';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .work-list-sm {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .work-list-sm li {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-ink-secondary);
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .work-list-sm li::before {
    content: '·';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  /* ── Hero CTAs ── */
  .hero-ctas {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .work-btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: var(--color-surface);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: opacity 0.15s;
    border: none;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .work-btn:hover { opacity: 0.85; }

  .work-link {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-tertiary);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }

  .work-link:hover { color: var(--color-accent); }

  /* ── Service labels ── */
  .service-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.5625rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .service-section-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.5625rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-ink-tertiary);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  /* ── Flagship ── */
  .service-flagship {
    padding: 1.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: var(--color-surface-secondary);
  }

  .service-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2.5vw, 1.4rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .service-prop {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-tertiary);
    font-style: italic;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .service-includes { }

  .service-includes-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.5625rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-ink-tertiary);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

